  "title": "Incomplete splitting-off in digraphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "mediawiki-wikitext",
    "text": "Given  a digraph ''D=(V+s,A)'' which is ''k''-arc-connected in ''V'', what is the maximum number of (disjoint) pairs of arcs, consisting of entering and leaving arcs at  <math>s</math>, whose (simultaneous) [[splitting off]] does not destroy the ''k''-arc-connectivity of ''D'' in ''V''?",
